<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Woolworths says unit gets ACCC okay.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Woolworths says unit gets ACCC okay.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woolworths Ltd said on Tuesday that the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission (ACCC) had approved the company's expansion on the grocery wholesaling business through its unit Independent Wholesalers Pty Ltd.</p>
<p>Woolworths said it made a submission to the ACCC.</p>
<p>&quot;The commission has now considered that submission, as well as a submission made on behalf of the Davids group and has advised that it does not propose to intervene in the matter pursuant to the Trade Practices Act,&quot; Woolworths said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
